WEBVTT

00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:06.000
Here’s how to run the two-circle team contract.

00:00:06.050 --> 00:00:08.158
Plan about sixty minutes.

00:00:08.208 --> 00:00:14.207
Draw two large circles on the wall, or use the canvas, and label them IN and OUT.

00:00:14.257 --> 00:00:19.762
Start with IN. Ask: “Think of a moment when this team was at its best.

00:00:19.812 --> 00:00:21.199
What were people doing?”

00:00:21.249 --> 00:00:24.747
Give everyone five minutes to write behaviours on post-its.

00:00:24.797 --> 00:00:28.013
One behaviour per post-it, starting with a verb. “Ask for help early.”

00:00:28.063 --> 00:00:29.555
“Share bad news quickly.”

00:00:29.605 --> 00:00:31.170
“Celebrate small wins.”

00:00:31.220 --> 00:00:33.191
Put them in the IN circle and read them out.

00:00:33.241 --> 00:00:35.908
Group the similar ones.

00:00:35.958 --> 00:00:44.632
Then do OUT. Ask: “What behaviours undermine trust, inclusion or good work in a team?” Notice the wording.

00:00:44.682 --> 00:00:49.933
You’re asking about behaviours in general, not about specific people.

00:00:49.983 --> 00:00:52.230
That makes it safer to write honestly.

00:00:52.280 --> 00:00:56.184
People will still write what they see in this team. That’s the point.

00:00:56.234 --> 00:00:59.604
Now comes the most important step: rewrite.

00:00:59.654 --> 00:01:04.874
Go through both circles and turn vague post-its into things someone could actually see.

00:01:04.924 --> 00:01:08.963
“Be respectful” becomes “No laptops when someone presents.”

00:01:09.013 --> 00:01:14.186
“Be open” becomes “Disagree in the meeting, not after it.”

00:01:14.236 --> 00:01:19.149
If you couldn’t tell whether someone is doing it, it’s not specific enough yet.

00:01:19.199 --> 00:01:24.049
Finally, reduce. Ask the team to choose the five to eight most important behaviours, using dots.

00:01:24.099 --> 00:01:28.523
A short contract that people remember is far better than a long one they don’t.

00:01:28.573 --> 00:01:31.454
End by asking: “Can everyone live with this?”

00:01:31.504 --> 00:01:35.135
And one more question: “What will we do when someone breaks it?”

00:01:35.185 --> 00:01:36.880
Agree on that now, while it’s easy.

